# why seaturtles make great software engineers 🐢

the seaturtle software manifesto:
1. 🐢 swim steady — slow, deliberate code; built for the long haul (80+ year lifespan → maintainable systems)
2. 🌊 stay wet — wait for 3+ usages before you extract; don't dry code too early
3. 🐡 wear shell — safe by default; retreat fast (fail-fast); guard clauses always there
4. 🐚 live shell — the terminal is home: cli, scripts, automation
5. 🤙 ride current — work with the system and its tools; know the critical path; minimal code
6. 🌙 follow moonlight — hatchlings follow the moon to the sea; follow conventions and good defaults
7. 🐢🐢🐢 turtles all the way — compose small pieces; recursion and composition over inheritance

> ocean vast, journey long, shell home. build software safe, steady, ready to dive. 🐢🌊🐚
